    "body": "This is similar to something we drafted in https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prerendering.html#delay-while-prerendering . If we can find enough specs that would use this then I'd be supportive. I suspect it might involve technically-backward-incompatible changes to exception ordering.\r\n\r\nI would prefer starting only with the Promise variant, although gathering data on what specs would use this might change my mind there.\r\n\r\nI don't understand why the type would need to be included in the arguments. I think you could just write in the spec for [Permission] \"If the return type of the operation is X, do Y.\"",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
